https://github.com/Ultra-Legacy-Hippeastrum/ims.

Developers and contributors credited by the upstream project:

Pierre-Hugues Husson (https://github.com/phhusson): original creator and core
IMS/SIP implementation.
Dominique Martinet (https://github.com/martinetd): SIP protocol, parsing,
transport, registration and IMS SMS development.
Mathias Gluszczynski (https://github.com/krazey): carrier policies,
registration recovery, signaling/media robustness and Android integration.
Aleksei Mikhasenko (https://github.com/amikhasenko): call handling, audio,
microphone fixes, reconnection behavior and platform integration.
Yaroslav Zviezda (https://github.com/acroreiser): legacy-device compatibility,
P-CSCF, registration/uplink fixes and Nexus reference work.
borbelyvince (https://github.com/borbelyvince): PLMN, subscription and SIP fixes.
derveror (https://github.com/derveror): Nexus 6P Android 15 integration,
Angler adaptation, device testing and maintenance.

Acknowledgements: every contributor and tester of the original PhhIms project,
Ultra Legacy Hippeastrum ports and wider legacy-device community.

The Nokia integration uses Soong, system_ext, platform APIs and the platform
certificate. It does not bundle an SDK, signing key, native AEC binary or
Gradle cache. Source copyright and license notices remain in their files.
